	"abilities": [
		"Velocity-sensitive keyboard",
		"Eight RGB pads",
		"Eight assignable encoders",
		"Scale and chord modes",
		"Arpeggiator",
		"USB and DIN MIDI"
	],
	"hardwareControls": [
		"WHEELS: Pitch, Modulation",
		"PADS: Pad 5, Pad 6, Pad 7, Pad 8, Pad 1, Pad 2, Pad 3, Pad 4",
		"SCREEN / NAVIGATION: Display, Menu, Bank -, Bank +, Plugin / DAW, Shift",
		"ENCODERS: Encoder 1, Encoder 2, Encoder 3, Encoder 4, Encoder 5, Encoder 6, Encoder 7, Encoder 8",
		"PERFORMANCE / TRANSPORT: Octave -, Octave +, Arp, Latch, Note repeat, Full level, Tap tempo, Program, Loop, Rewind, Forward, Stop, Play, Record"
	],
	"notice": "Use the MIDI performance port for notes, pads and wheels; use the DAW port only with the matching DAW script. Configure pads and encoders in Program Edit on the hardware. Set Globals > DINsrc to INT for internal performance data or USB for computer-to-DIN routing. This generation has wheels and a DIN output; it is distinct from MPK mini MK3. Pad notes and encoder assignments are editable. Virtual key notes are a chromatic reference; check octave, scale and chord modes. Select the profile manually if the host does not identify it: no unverified port aliases are supplied. Diagrams are original simplified schematics, not scale drawings. Physical controls without a binding are informational; use MIDI learn for configurable assignments.",
